in @optics

# @optics/source — the active-facet sub-family.
#
# Sub-prism under @optics declaring the species that carry energy
# into the beam (gain media, emitters). Per docs/specs/optical-
# keywords.md §1.7, a `source` declares an ACTIVE FACET: all facet
# declarations apply, plus the `active` energy bit and the
# `source_declares_energy_balance` property (§3.9) which gates the
# declaration by requiring pumping mechanism + gain curve +
# saturation behaviour.
#
# === Species under this sub-family ===
#
#   @optics/source/ganglion  the 5 per-ganglion gain media of
#                              Fate's connectome. Recognition #58
#                              Surface B closure: each ganglion's
#                              `infer` walk is energy injection from
#                              @io; this sub-family declares each
#                              ganglion's effective gain curve as a
#                              source declaration.
#
# Per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]: `glass @optics/
# source { ... }` declares this IS a sub-prism of @optics. Per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]] / `keyword_matches_depth`, depth-1
# specializations use `glass` (not `prism`); the keyword tracks the
# Bateson level (recognition #51).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §1.7 (source keyword),
#               §3.9 (source_declares_energy_balance property),
#               §4.9 (@kintsugi/fracture/source_energy — missing
#               fields surface as @io ticks per substrate-pull
#               discipline).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                      (recognition #57; energy injection IS the @io
#                      boundary crossing per §9.3).
# Related shards: optics.mirror (parent family root),
#                 optics/source/ganglion.mirror (the per-ganglion
#                 sub-family this tick lands).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/optics/source.mirror`
# declares `@optics/source` as the sub-family root; species live at
# `shards/optics/source/<name>.mirror`.

glass @optics/source {
  focus source
  project source
  split source
  shift source
  settle source
}

out @optics/source
